1
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:03,600
You've been going here and there
around here for a while.

2
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:06,440
Work. I've got three orders
for campus errand runs.

3
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:11,520
Using this?

4
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:14,200
A junior lent it to me.

5
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,080
I'll get going.

6
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:29,040
Get off.

7
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,200
I should've taken more orders.

8
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:39,800
Take your time.

9
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,920
I can take you around
a few laps every day.

10
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:47,560
By the way, I just left the lab,

11
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:49,240
and I saw Xie Yudi being called in.

12
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,440
Why isn't the dean here today?

13
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:59,200
Does the university really care so little
about me getting beaten up?

14
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:01,160
Regarding the fight,

15
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,320
we've spoken to several witnesses.

16
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:05,400
They all said you were the one
who started it.

17
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,360
So you can just ask a few students
and then pass judgment?

18
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:09,440
Xie Yudi.

19
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,760
Besides Chen Yanzhou,
have you ever bullied any other students?

20
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,080
Ma'am, I've never bullied anyone.

21
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:18,680
But people are saying

22
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:22,120
you bullied classmates
back in high school,

23
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,400
and that behavior continued into--

24
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,640
You mean Zhuang Ning, right?

25
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,000
I don't understand why
everyone thinks that.

26
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,240
She and I are from the same hometown.

27
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,760
We're very close.

28
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,280
That's right.

29
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,920
I only learned about

30
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,040
the condition of Zheng Yu's mom
because Zhuang Ning told me.

31
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:46,280
I couldn't think of any other way to help,

32
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:49,640
so I came up with
the idea of a fundraiser.

33
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,920
If I'd been bullying her all this time,

34
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:55,960
would she still
share these things with me?

35
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,000
Are you saying

36
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:10,360
you learned everything about Zheng Yu
from Zhuang Ning?

37
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:14,320
Well, not entirely.

38
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,120
I'd known for a long time

39
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,760
that Zheng Yu was having a hard time.

40
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:23,040
I'd lent her money
and recommended a hospital to her.

41
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:26,400
Later, I found out
she was Zhuang Ning's roommate,

42
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,160
which made me feel even closer to her.

43
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,960
You can ask Zheng Yu about that yourself.

44
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:34,880
If you're worried about hurting her pride,

45
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:36,320
I have the transfer records here.

46
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:39,400
As for Zhuang Ning, that's even simpler.

47
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,600
Just call her in and ask her yourselves.

48
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,320
Your word alone isn't enough.

49
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:50,120
Zhuang Ning
has been waiting next door for a while.

50
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:14,840
Sit down.

51
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,600
Have a seat.

52
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,400
Come on.

53
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:28,360
That's great. Now you can
get to the bottom of this.

54
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:31,520
Can the university issue an
official statement or something afterward?

55
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:33,800
When Chen Yanzhou was accused of cheating,

56
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,200
the university cleared his name.

57
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,240
The accusations against me

58
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:38,320
are far more serious.

59
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,200
Zhuang Ning. Mr. Song has probably
told you everything Xie Yudi said.

60
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,080
Is what he said true?

61
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,040
It's true.

62
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:57,760
I've told him a lot about Zheng Yu.

63
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:00,120
Zhuang Ning is
a pretty introverted person,

64
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,600
and she doesn't have many friends here.

65
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,680
So she could only talk to an old classmate
like me about dorm matters.

66
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:12,400
I told him when Zheng Yu
would be in the dorm,

67
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:15,920
when she'd go to her part-time job,
which classes she'd chosen,

68
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,680
and how many words she'd exchanged
with male classmates.

69
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:20,360
- Zhuang Ning.
- What color she was wearing…

70
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,720
What are you talking about?

71
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:29,440
What's wrong?

72
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,600
Aren't we old classmates?

73
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,880
We talk all the time
and share things with each other.

74
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:38,880
And that's not all.

75
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,360
We used to hang out together
all the time too.

76
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,960
I, ZHUANG NING, FORMALLY REPORT
MY CLASSMATE, XIE YUDI.

77
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:25,880
What are you doing?

78
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,920
Xie Yudi, what's with that attitude?

79
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,440
You have some nerve.

80
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:34,960
As you said,

81
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:37,240
we're adults now, after all.

82
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,560
<i>We're adults now, after all.</i>

83
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:52,960
Xie Yudi!

84
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:55,680
Xie Yudi, stop right there!

85
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,280
Zhuang Ning.

86
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,160
You can go back for now.

87
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:10,000
The college will make sure
this is properly addressed.

88
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,240
Ma'am.

89
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:16,000
I have one more thing to give you.

90
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:22,040
I wonder how this whole thing
will eventually be handled.

91
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,920
Can I ask you what happened
between you and Xie Yudi?

92
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:37,799
He was the first person I met here.

93
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:44,800
<i>We added each other on WeChat</i>
<i>at the start of our freshman year.</i>

94
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:45,760
XIE YUDI

95
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,280
<i>Zheng Yu.</i>

96
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,480
<i>Why are your eyes so red?</i>

97
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:55,720
I got dust in my eyes in the stairwell.

98
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,360
By the way, how's Mom doing?

99
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:03,560
The doctor said her condition is stable
for now, so don't worry.

100
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,360
There are plenty of hospitals in Qingyi,

101
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:13,280
but none can take a patient
who's been unconscious for this long

102
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,760
on a long-term basis.

103
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:16,720
Let me keep looking.

104
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:19,280
Transferring hospitals
will cost a lot, right?

105
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,520
Just focus on preparing for your exams.

106
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:27,360
<i>Don't end up</i>
<i>not getting into a school here.</i>

107
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:29,960
As for Mom…

108
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,200
I won't leave her there

109
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:36,400
all alone.

110
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,080
All right.

111
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,400
Goodbye for now.

112
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,000
Are you the freshman representative
from the College of Life Sciences

113
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,840
who gave a speech at orientation?

114
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:40,080
I'm in Life Sciences Class 1 too.

115
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:42,600
I'm here to take some footage
for our PR department.

116
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,880
Hi there.

117
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,160
There's a hospital near our university
called Ji Heng.

118
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:57,480
It has its own rehab center

119
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,920
and can accommodate patients
in a vegetative state long-term.

120
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:01,960
Ji Heng is a private hospital.

121
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:04,560
Right, it is pretty expensive.

122
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:07,640
But still, you should look into it.

123
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:10,720
It was recently added
to the list of approved medical providers,

124
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:13,080
so some costs can be covered by insurance.

125
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:17,680
Also, they run a program called
Compassionate Care Bed.

126
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:19,960
You can try applying.

127
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:23,080
If you manage to secure a spot,
you'll get a partial fee discount.

128
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:26,080
Compassionate Care Bed?

129
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:27,920
I've never heard of it.

130
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,760
There are very few spots,
so it's not widely advertised.

131
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,920
It's all about having access
to the right information.

132
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:37,680
If you still can't find
another solution for now,

133
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:40,200
I can lend you some money.

134
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:43,640
Then at least you could
move your mom here first.

135
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,840
It's fine.

136
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,920
We'll be classmates for four years.

137
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,440
It's not like you're going to run away.

138
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,320
Come to me if you need anything.
I won't run away either.

139
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,640
Bye.

140
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:27,800
<i>All I wanted at the time</i>
<i>was to bring my mom over.</i>

141
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,560
<i>I didn't have time to think.</i>

142
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:30,520
NEW FRIEND
XIE YUDI

143
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,320
<i>I had my doubts,</i>

144
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:35,760
<i>but something else happened soon after</i>
<i>that made me let my guard down.</i>

145
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,440
<i>Are you crazy?</i>

146
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,360
JIANG HAIXIN

147
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,480
<i>You took your mom away</i>
<i>without even telling me!</i>

148
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:45,160
<i>Wu and the others didn't see your mom</i>
<i>at the hospital and thought you'd run,</i>

149
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,400
<i>so they've been harassing me</i>
<i>with calls every day!</i>

150
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,480
<i>How am I supposed</i>
<i>to run my business like this?</i>

151
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,320
<i>And don't contact Xiaomian anymore, okay?</i>

152
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,480
<i>You're distracting him from his studies.</i>

153
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:00,800
Zheng Yu.

154
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,160
I have good news.

155
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:09,160
Starting next month,

156
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:12,800
your mom will be eligible
for the Compassionate Care Bed program.

157
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,280
Really?

158
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:18,360
After you told me about it,
I went to ask around.

159
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:22,160
They said there are very few spots,
and lots of people apply for them.

160
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,600
Trust me, I wouldn't lie to you.

161
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:27,840
But once your mom gets a spot,

162
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:31,920
make sure you don't talk to anyone else
at the hospital about it.

163
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:40,800
The reason I know Ji Heng so well

164
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:42,720
is that my uncle

165
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:46,120
is the director of
the hospital's rehab center.

166
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:48,560
Please keep this between us.

167
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:49,920
I don't want to get him in trouble.

168
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:54,560
Are you

169
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,160
uncomfortable with doing this?

170
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:03,160
Trying to take the moral high ground now
would just make me look more ridiculous.

171
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,080
Hello?

172
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:11,200
Dr. Zhao?

173
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,360
All right.

174
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:14,840
I understand.

175
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:18,840
I really got it.

176
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:27,400
<i>Maybe it was because I accepted</i>
<i>that unfairly allocated spot</i>

177
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:30,360
<i>that I later suffered</i>
<i>all those consequences.</i>

178
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,040
XIE YUDI

179
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:38,120
<i>You've got a grain of rice on your chin.</i>

180
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:02,520
My tumbler.

181
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:18,400
Your tumbler
doesn't keep drinks warm at all.

182
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:19,840
I'll buy you a new one.

183
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,480
Why did you block me?

184
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,480
I've paid back all the money I owed you.

185
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,720
I won't need to transfer money to you
on WeChat anymore.

186
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:42,040
What happened to your hand?

187
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:45,720
It's nothing.

188
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:49,280
I sent friend requests from an alt account
so many times, but you never accepted.

189
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,960
Time feels so slow,

190
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:52,600
so every hour,

191
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,560
I just feel like cutting here.

192
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:01,880
What happened after that?

193
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:06,040
I later realized
that was only the beginning.

194
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:09,400
He threatened to jump off a building,
throw himself in front of a train,

195
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:10,840
and cut off his fingers.

196
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:17,680
All of it was just his way
of trying to make me obey him.

197
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:19,720
But to avoid more trouble…

198
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:20,960
No.

199
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,440
The truth is,

200
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:26,880
I didn't want to lose the hospital spot,
so I put up with it.

201
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,080
It seems I should've hit him
a few more times.

202
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:38,760
You've done everything you could.

203
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:41,360
And I've done everything I could too.

204
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:48,560
I have something to do. I'll get going.

205
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:59,880
Goodness! Good thing I ran fast.

206
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:02,000
It started raining
just as I reached the dorm.

207
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:06,359
Oh, right.

208
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:10,079
The pharmacist said
you can't take more than two pills a day,

209
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,280
so don't take too many.

210
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:18,319
Do you think things worked out
for Zhuang Ning?

211
00:17:20,119 --> 00:17:22,680
You're in so much pain,
and you're still thinking about that?

212
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:24,440
I did my part, after all.

213
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,720
It should work out.

214
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:29,360
I hope so.

215
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:30,720
It definitely will!

216
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:34,480
By the way, what did you say just now?

217
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:35,960
"It definitely will."

218
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:38,520
No, what did you say when you came in?

219
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:40,320
It's raining.

220
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:58,920
Zhuang Ning.

221
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:08,760
I'm going the same way.

222
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:10,720
Thank you.

223
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,520
Let's go.

224
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,080
Zhuang Ning.

225
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:21,680
A certain young lady said
you'd catch a cold if you got soaked,

226
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:23,280
so she insisted I come get you.

227
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,640
So are you hungry?

228
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:34,960
Fangli.

229
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:35,880
TWELVE HOURS AGO

230
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:38,800
I just got their Hometown Association
Registration Forms from Zhang Qi.

231
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,960
It turns out Zhuang Ning…

232
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:42,520
She was Xie Yudi's high school classmate.

233
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,400
REPORT LETTER

234
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:57,280
SUPPRESSING A HEAVY AND FEARFUL HEART,

235
00:18:57,360 --> 00:19:00,240
BUT COMPELLED BY THE NEED TO SEEK JUSTICE…

236
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,920
This one's not good. Use mine.

237
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,320
Here's my brightest red lipstick to press
for your fingerprint when you're done.

238
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:19,280
Zheng Yu, when did you get back?

239
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:20,480
Just now.

240
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:24,000
Chen Yanzhou and I got the contact details
of the owner of the base where we stayed.

241
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:25,880
They have security footage
of the activity room.

242
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:28,640
Also, I sent you a copy of a chat history.

243
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,680
It should come in handy.

244
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:33,520
Zheng Yu, you're amazing!

245
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:35,160
Seriously, you're incredible!

246
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,200
Let's see.

247
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:05,440
We still have to wait for the outcome,

248
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,200
but even so,

249
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:10,200
I feel so much lighter now.

250
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:13,080
That's good.

251
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:15,520
Let's go back to the dorm
and take a shower.

252
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:18,360
Whoever gets back first showers first.

253
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:20,680
- Three, two…
- Liu Linlin, that's cheating!

254
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,080
Zheng Yu, let's run!

255
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,880
<i>Is everyone free this weekend?</i>

256
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,800
<i>Let's go out for a nice meal together.</i>

257
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:38,800
<i>I'm in! I've been craving a fancy meal!</i>

258
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:39,800
<i>I have no problem.</i>

259
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,120
<i>What about Zheng Yu?</i>

260
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,920
<i>I'll be free after my part-time job,</i>
<i>but it'll be a bit late.</i>

261
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:02,760
HAVE YOU HEARD?

262
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:05,680
XYD FROM LIFE SCIENCES WAS CAUGHT
BULLYING A GIRL IN HIS CLASS.

263
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:34,840
DAD

264
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:41,800
<i>Sign the papers.</i>

265
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:44,200
<i>You just need to complete</i>
<i>all the withdrawal procedures.</i>

266
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:47,080
<i>The police have opened a case.</i>

267
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,400
<i>They'll contact you as needed.</i>

268
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:51,800
<i>Keep your phone on after you leave,</i>
<i>and report to the police when summoned.</i>

269
00:21:52,560 --> 00:21:55,520
<i>The university will fully cooperate with</i>
<i>the investigation. You should too.</i>

270
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:56,600
That's all.

271
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,680
Thank you, ma'am.

272
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:02,000
Thank you for handling this.
I know it's been a lot of work.

273
00:22:02,080 --> 00:22:03,120
It's no trouble.

274
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:05,080
Thank you for your understanding
and cooperation.

275
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:19,120
Don't ask me why I didn't save you.

276
00:22:19,920 --> 00:22:22,680
I don't think you should
keep studying here.

277
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:23,840
Yes.

278
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:24,800
Once again,

279
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:26,680
you've disappointed me.

280
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:12,000
DELETE CONTACT?

281
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:16,080
XIE YUDI

282
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:18,680
BLOCK?

283
00:23:18,760 --> 00:23:20,680
ADD TO BLACKLIST
CONFIRM?

284
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:21,640
SAVING

285
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:11,560
Class dismissed.

286
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:17,280
What job did you take this time?

287
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:18,680
Is it difficult?

288
00:24:22,560 --> 00:24:23,760
It's not work.

289
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,640
You're going out to eat with someone?

290
00:24:29,360 --> 00:24:31,320
- Who?
- My roommates.

291
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:37,520
Do you know any good restaurants?

292
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:41,000
Forget it. You don't live on campus
or have many friends.

293
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:43,320
You probably don't know
the good food spots near campus.

294
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:46,160
Fine.

295
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,120
Take your time looking.

296
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:49,960
Since I have no friends
and don't live on campus, I'll leave now.

297
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:52,000
Are you mad?

298
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:54,240
No.

299
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:56,400
You have people to eat with,

300
00:24:56,480 --> 00:24:57,600
and so do I.

301
00:24:57,680 --> 00:24:58,760
Bye.

302
00:25:03,160 --> 00:25:04,240
Who?

303
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,320
Their signature dishes are
pineapple fried rice,

304
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:10,320
massaman curry, and coconut chicken soup.

305
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:12,760
They also have drunken noodles,
but those contain chili.

306
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:15,560
If you think choosing is too much trouble,
you can order a meal set.

307
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:17,440
They have a set for four.

308
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:19,600
You know the menu so well.
Have you eaten here?

309
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:21,520
No. I looked it up before coming.

310
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:24,760
Then let's get the set for four.

311
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:29,520
One meal set for four.
And a dozen beers.

312
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:31,320
Isn't a dozen a bit much?

313
00:25:31,920 --> 00:25:33,040
I'll drink them if you won't.

314
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:36,360
Drink up.

315
00:25:42,120 --> 00:25:43,680
Thanks for your help last time.

316
00:25:43,760 --> 00:25:45,960
I didn't keep it from your mom
just to help you out.

317
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:47,880
I didn't want her to worry about you.

318
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:50,560
Still, thank you.

319
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:54,000
Did you read the email I sent you?

320
00:25:54,640 --> 00:25:57,280
The one about the internship
at the German research institute?

321
00:25:57,360 --> 00:25:58,720
Let's break it down.

322
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:03,560
The paper you've been wanting to work on
the most has already been submitted.

323
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:07,240
By senior year, you'll barely have any
classes left, and our college's policy

324
00:26:07,320 --> 00:26:09,000
gives you credits for internships.

325
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:12,440
Given our university's ranking
and your GPA,

326
00:26:12,520 --> 00:26:15,440
applying to this institute in the second
half of the year will be perfect timing.

327
00:26:17,440 --> 00:26:19,200
It's a cancer research project.

328
00:26:19,920 --> 00:26:21,080
So you did read it.

329
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:23,680
What's wrong with cancer research?

330
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:26,280
I'd still rather study plants.

331
00:26:39,600 --> 00:26:40,800
Your brother's gone.

332
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:44,600
Your mom has lost her memory.

333
00:26:44,680 --> 00:26:46,520
Your dad just does whatever you say.

334
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:49,240
Looks like I'm the only one
who still remembers

335
00:26:49,320 --> 00:26:51,080
that your dream used to be
becoming a doctor.

336
00:26:58,560 --> 00:27:01,000
Go back and prepare your resume.
Give the application a shot.

337
00:27:01,080 --> 00:27:04,280
That institute has very high standards.
There's no guarantee you'll get in.

338
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:08,160
It's going to rain.

339
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:11,760
You should head back soon.
I only have one umbrella.

340
00:27:22,320 --> 00:27:24,560
Hey, take it easy on the drinks.

341
00:27:24,640 --> 00:27:27,440
Eat something to line your stomach.
Don't just drink all night.

342
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:31,680
No, no.

343
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:34,280
There's still food there.

344
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:36,040
- I want hers.
- You…

345
00:27:36,120 --> 00:27:37,400
I'll order you a fresh bowl.

346
00:27:37,480 --> 00:27:38,800
I still remember

347
00:27:39,360 --> 00:27:41,920
how, back when
we first moved into Room 223,

348
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,960
I asked to buy some of your food,
but you wouldn't sell.

349
00:27:44,640 --> 00:27:46,560
And you still won't share with me.

350
00:27:48,840 --> 00:27:49,960
Have you had too much to drink?

351
00:27:50,040 --> 00:27:51,640
How can you hold a grudge for so long?

352
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,440
There. Happy now?

353
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:13,560
Yes.

354
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:20,160
So how is it?
Does leftover food taste good?

355
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:25,920
- I'm not eating it. I don't want any!
- Try some. Just a bite!

356
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:27,080
You eat it.

357
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:29,520
Come on, eat it. You eat it.

358
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:30,640
Zhuang Ning.

359
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:32,760
- Try it! It's really good!
- No, no.

360
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:34,200
- You eat more.
- You eat more.

361
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:35,680
- You eat.
- I'm not eating it.

362
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:36,640
You eat all of it.

363
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:40,800
Yours is all burnt! Just try another bite!

364
00:28:40,880 --> 00:28:43,920
- One more bite!
- Just eat it. I'm not eating it.

365
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,440
You all know

366
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:47,960
that I work part-time
at a convenience store.

367
00:28:48,040 --> 00:28:50,920
The shelf life of their boxed meals
is 36 hours.

368
00:28:52,280 --> 00:28:54,920
The first 12 hours
are for production and delivery to stores.

369
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:58,280
The remaining 24 hours
are the selling period.

370
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:01,480
What are you trying to say?

371
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:05,520
The night you moved in,

372
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:07,040
my boxed meal had expired.

373
00:29:08,160 --> 00:29:10,800
I was embarrassed,
so I didn't give it to you.

374
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:17,480
Back then, the day of the Sports Meet,

375
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:20,720
I didn't accept the shoes you gave me

376
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:25,240
because I was afraid
that when your birthdays came around,

377
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:27,440
I wouldn't be able
to get you gifts in return.

378
00:29:27,520 --> 00:29:29,560
I used to turn down meals with you

379
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:31,760
because I couldn't afford to pay my share.

380
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:33,280
I didn't want to freeload.

381
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:38,160
Maintaining friendships
costs too much money for me.

382
00:29:40,080 --> 00:29:41,680
Sometimes, I really envy you guys.

383
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:51,440
I envy you too.

384
00:29:56,560 --> 00:29:57,600
Actually,

385
00:29:58,360 --> 00:30:00,120
I'm not bothered by light when I sleep.

386
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:03,800
And when you study at night,

387
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:05,760
your desk lamp isn't bright at all.

388
00:30:09,280 --> 00:30:11,440
It's seeing how hard you work
that keeps me awake.

389
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:14,400
Do you know

390
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:16,200
how intimidating
it is for someone like me,

391
00:30:16,280 --> 00:30:18,560
who spent years diligently studying

392
00:30:18,640 --> 00:30:20,640
and still barely managed
to get into this university,

393
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:24,800
to room with someone like you?

394
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:30,320
Linlin.

395
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:31,800
Have you had too much to drink too?

396
00:30:32,840 --> 00:30:34,080
And you!

397
00:30:35,040 --> 00:30:38,280
In life, you have to be good
at either studying or having fun.

398
00:30:38,360 --> 00:30:39,680
You're really good at having fun.

399
00:30:39,760 --> 00:30:42,840
Why do I feel like
that's not a compliment?

400
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:47,080
But if you want to have fun, I'll take you
along wherever I go from now on.

401
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:50,920
Linlin. You're already amazing.

402
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:54,440
You don't have to comfort me. I'm saying
this because I've thought it through.

403
00:30:56,080 --> 00:30:57,880
Growing up, people always told us

404
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:59,480
that everyone has a purpose in life.

405
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:02,560
But as we got older,
we realized we're just expendable.

406
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:09,600
The truth is, most of us in this world
are probably just disposable.

407
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:16,240
Then let's toast

408
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:18,040
to being expendable!

409
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:19,520
Sure!

410
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:21,800
- To being expendable!
- To being expendable!

411
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:28,320
To the future!

412
00:31:28,840 --> 00:31:30,200
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

413
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:11,440
Did Xu Fangli drink so much
that she passed out in the restroom?

414
00:32:13,120 --> 00:32:14,520
Linlin's with her. Don't worry.

415
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:23,800
Zheng Yu.

416
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:28,960
This is for you.

417
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:34,840
"Rain."

418
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:37,760
"Zhuangzi's Butterfly Dream."

419
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:46,840
VICTORY WON'T COME TO ME
UNLESS I GO TO IT

420
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:56,760
<i>1,800 is already a bargain.</i>
<i>I can't go any lower.</i>

421
00:32:57,680 --> 00:32:58,880
<i>All right.</i>

422
00:32:58,960 --> 00:33:00,240
<i>Are you sure you want it?</i>

423
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:04,160
<i>Which dorm building do you live in?</i>
<i>Which room?</i>

424
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:07,040
<i>I can deliver it to you.</i>
<i>We'll do the exchange in person.</i>

425
00:33:07,120 --> 00:33:09,520
ZHUANGZI'S BUTTERFLY DREAM

426
00:33:09,600 --> 00:33:10,520
<i>Sure.</i>

427
00:33:11,080 --> 00:33:13,200
<i>I live in Room 223 of Sixian Hall.</i>

428
00:33:31,320 --> 00:33:33,320
<i>I'm too far away from you.</i>

429
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:36,280
<i>How about leaving it</i>
<i>in the library locker?</i>

430
00:33:37,080 --> 00:33:37,920
<i>Okay.</i>

431
00:33:42,360 --> 00:33:43,960
<i>I just remembered something.</i>

432
00:33:44,040 --> 00:33:47,280
<i>I put stickers on my laptop.</i>
<i>There's a string of English words on them.</i>

433
00:33:47,360 --> 00:33:50,520
<i>The adhesive is pretty strong,</i>
<i>so I'll take another 200 off.</i>

434
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:55,160
Why didn't you tell me back then

435
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:56,840
that you were the one
who sold me the laptop?

436
00:33:58,320 --> 00:34:01,440
Because I was judging you
by my own standards.

437
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:04,480
I was worried you'd feel embarrassed
buying secondhand.

438
00:34:05,120 --> 00:34:07,040
But after getting to know you,

439
00:34:07,840 --> 00:34:09,480
I realized I was overthinking it.

440
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:11,960
Thank you.

441
00:34:14,159 --> 00:34:15,520
You're the one who helped me.

442
00:34:27,639 --> 00:34:29,239
<i>Your brother's gone.</i>

443
00:34:30,480 --> 00:34:32,400
<i>Your mother has lost her memory.</i>

444
00:34:33,520 --> 00:34:35,120
<i>Your dad just does whatever you say.</i>

445
00:34:36,040 --> 00:34:37,760
<i>Looks like I'm the only one</i>
<i>who still remembers</i>

446
00:34:37,840 --> 00:34:39,880
<i>that your dream used to be</i>
<i>becoming a doctor.</i>

447
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:34,840
It's the rainy season.
It starts raining before you know it.

448
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:37,480
Even I forgot my umbrella.
I wonder if those two brought theirs.

449
00:35:40,200 --> 00:35:42,560
Isn't that Chen Yanzhou?

450
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:49,040
What a coincidence.
You two are eating here?

451
00:35:49,120 --> 00:35:51,920
What are you doing here?
Didn't you have plans with someone?

452
00:35:53,360 --> 00:35:55,200
I just finished eating
and was heading home.

453
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:56,720
Excuse me.

454
00:35:56,800 --> 00:36:00,040
Where have all the handsome guys
in the world gone?

455
00:36:00,120 --> 00:36:02,320
They're all waiting for you
in the dorm! Let's go.

456
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:06,640
Chen Yanzhou.

457
00:36:09,360 --> 00:36:12,120
Why are you standing so close to Zheng Yu?

458
00:36:13,760 --> 00:36:16,280
Let me tell you, he's a bad guy.
A really terrible one!

459
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:19,080
I asked him for a bottle of water at
the Sports Meet, and he said no.

460
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:21,680
I'm a whole person,
yet I'm worth less than a bottle of water!

461
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,600
Fangli.

462
00:36:23,680 --> 00:36:24,840
Our ride is here.

463
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:26,760
Here.

464
00:36:28,480 --> 00:36:29,520
I'll go first.

465
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:32,600
Come on.

466
00:36:35,120 --> 00:36:36,440
Get in.

467
00:36:36,520 --> 00:36:37,360
Oh gosh.

468
00:36:38,720 --> 00:36:39,640
I'll get going.

469
00:36:40,240 --> 00:36:41,160
I…

470
00:36:41,880 --> 00:36:43,440
I'll walk you to the car.

471
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:51,200
Fangli, move over.
There's no room for Zheng Yu.

472
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:55,480
Why is this Ferrari so small?
I can't even stretch my legs!

473
00:36:55,560 --> 00:36:57,480
Oh gosh.

474
00:36:58,160 --> 00:37:00,640
I actually have something to do
and need to stop by the lab.

475
00:37:01,920 --> 00:37:03,840
Let's just make do and walk back.

476
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:07,360
Then I'll leave Zheng Yu in your hands.

477
00:37:17,200 --> 00:37:18,040
Let's go.

478
00:37:23,600 --> 00:37:25,360
Didn't you just say

479
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:27,720
you were going home after your date?

480
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:29,560
Why are you suddenly going to the lab?

481
00:37:30,760 --> 00:37:31,600
A date?

482
00:37:34,280 --> 00:37:36,440
You mean me and Li Yanan?

483
00:37:38,600 --> 00:37:41,400
So you were having dinner with Mr. Li.

484
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:45,880
I was going home,

485
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:48,760
but then I remembered
I forgot to change the water in the trays.

486
00:37:48,840 --> 00:37:51,600
All those plants in the lab
are waiting for me to take care of them.

487
00:37:51,680 --> 00:37:53,000
What about you?

488
00:37:53,080 --> 00:37:54,880
How did your date go?

489
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:57,000
It was strange.

490
00:37:57,640 --> 00:38:01,520
There were things I didn't want to say
for all sorts of reasons before.

491
00:38:01,600 --> 00:38:03,040
Today, I finally said them all.

492
00:38:03,720 --> 00:38:07,480
Is it really better to say the things
you don't want to say?

493
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:10,400
I'm not sure if things are really better,

494
00:38:11,560 --> 00:38:13,720
but it wasn't as hard as I thought.

495
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:17,120
And after I said everything,
everyone felt closer.

496
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:20,360
What about you?

497
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:23,160
Is there something
you've been hiding and haven't said?

498
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:27,520
Watch your step.

499
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:06,160
Hold on a second.

500
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:14,520
- You didn't get wet at all.
- What are you doing?

501
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:19,000
I left you behind earlier,
so I felt a little bad.

502
00:39:19,080 --> 00:39:23,160
So I wanted to see
if your knight in shining armor

503
00:39:23,240 --> 00:39:24,800
had done his job properly.

504
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:26,920
How childish.

505
00:39:27,720 --> 00:39:28,760
So childish!

506
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:32,040
I still want another drink.

507
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:33,080
Stop drinking.

508
00:39:33,160 --> 00:39:34,120
Go to sleep.

509
00:39:39,080 --> 00:39:39,920
Zheng Yu.

510
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:42,880
Do you want to hear the gossip
about Fangli meeting a hot guy tonight?

511
00:39:45,200 --> 00:39:46,480
Zheng Yu.

512
00:39:48,680 --> 00:39:49,520
Zheng Yu.

513
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:53,400
Zhuang Ning.

514
00:39:54,120 --> 00:39:55,960
- Let's make a bet.
- About what?

515
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:58,720
That Chen Yanzhou likes Zheng Yu.

516
00:39:59,520 --> 00:40:02,400
I started suspecting it when they worked
together during the Excellence Cup.

517
00:40:03,240 --> 00:40:07,000
Honestly, that's not much of a bet.

518
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:09,920
You noticed it too?

519
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:11,520
Everyone's noticed it.

520
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:25,280
ALLELES: DOMINANT AND RECESSIVE

521
00:41:36,120 --> 00:41:38,360
<i>Looks like your practical skills</i>
<i>aren't that great either.</i>

522
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:40,240
<i>How did you let</i>
<i>these bellflowers get so bad?</i>

523
00:41:40,320 --> 00:41:42,600
ZHENG YU

524
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:47,520
<i>What brings you to the hospital?</i>

525
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:57,240
Ms. Yang messaged me
asking me to come save this plant.

526
00:41:57,320 --> 00:41:59,560
Look, she even trusts me…

527
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:09,680
Xiaochen.

528
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:10,880
Ms. Yang.

529
00:42:10,960 --> 00:42:13,160
You're Chen Yanzhou?

530
00:42:17,400 --> 00:42:18,560
Xiaomian.

531
00:42:18,640 --> 00:42:19,840
What brings you here today?

532
00:42:20,920 --> 00:42:22,040
My exams are over,

533
00:42:22,120 --> 00:42:24,560
so I came to show my grades
to my sister and Mom.

534
00:42:28,440 --> 00:42:30,320
Don't just stand there.

535
00:42:31,640 --> 00:42:34,480
Since my sister isn't here,
I'll get going.

536
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:56,160
Here's my contact info.

537
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:58,880
If anything happens and you can't reach
your sister, you can contact me.

538
00:42:58,960 --> 00:43:00,200
Are you that close to my sister?

539
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:03,880
Otherwise, why would I be here?

540
00:43:03,960 --> 00:43:06,640
I won't contact you,
so stop meddling in my business.

541
00:43:07,880 --> 00:43:10,440
Even if you're close to her,
you and I aren't close.

542
00:43:25,440 --> 00:43:26,560
He's still young,

543
00:43:27,200 --> 00:43:28,480
but he's got quite a temper.

544
00:43:30,640 --> 00:43:34,000
CORE INTRODUCTION
TO REHABILITATION THERAPY

545
00:43:42,240 --> 00:43:46,440
<i>Maybe it was because</i>
<i>I accepted that unfairly allocated spot</i>

546
00:43:46,520 --> 00:43:49,080
<i>that I later suffered</i>
<i>all those consequences.</i>

547
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:56,360
DOCTOR TEAM
XIE LIMING, ZHANG HUIMIN

548
00:44:00,760 --> 00:44:02,520
Why didn't you reply to my message?

549
00:44:02,600 --> 00:44:03,960
What are you looking at?

550
00:44:07,760 --> 00:44:08,640
What's wrong?

551
00:44:08,720 --> 00:44:10,360
As far as I remember,

552
00:44:10,440 --> 00:44:12,200
Zhuang Ning is from Hengjiang.

553
00:44:14,160 --> 00:44:15,600
Hengjiang High School.

554
00:44:15,680 --> 00:44:17,160
She and Xie Yudi are from the same place.

555
00:44:21,120 --> 00:44:23,360
Director Xie is from Shaoyang.

556
00:44:23,440 --> 00:44:25,560
How could his nephew be from Hengjiang?

557
00:44:26,160 --> 00:44:27,480
Those places are so far apart.

558
00:44:27,560 --> 00:44:30,040
Maybe the family moved.

559
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:33,280
They may live in different places,
but they're still blood relatives.

560
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:37,960
People can move wherever they want,
but their hometown doesn't change.

561
00:44:48,440 --> 00:44:49,560
Xiaozheng, you're here.

562
00:44:50,240 --> 00:44:54,320
Xiaochen, what was the ratio
for that nutrient solution again?

563
00:44:55,280 --> 00:44:56,760
I'll help you mix it at the water station.

564
00:44:56,840 --> 00:44:57,800
All right.

565
00:45:03,440 --> 00:45:05,000
Zheng Yu, perfect timing.

566
00:45:05,080 --> 00:45:07,560
This is this year's
Compassionate Care Bed application form.

567
00:45:07,640 --> 00:45:09,120
You were so eager before.

568
00:45:09,200 --> 00:45:11,640
Now that applications are open,
why haven't you said anything?

569
00:45:12,880 --> 00:45:15,480
My eligibility to apply
hasn't been revoked?

570
00:45:15,560 --> 00:45:18,120
What do you mean?
Why would we revoke it for no reason?

571
00:45:21,200 --> 00:45:22,440
I have a question.

572
00:45:23,320 --> 00:45:26,240
Does Director Xie have a nephew?

573
00:45:26,320 --> 00:45:27,200
Yes.

574
00:45:28,760 --> 00:45:31,920
He even attended his nephew's
one-month celebration last month.

575
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:34,320
I covered his shift that day.
Why do you ask?

576
00:45:42,160 --> 00:45:45,280
I thought back then that the reason
I got this bed was because…

577
00:45:48,400 --> 00:45:51,000
Isn't the spot
for the program hard to get?

578
00:45:51,080 --> 00:45:53,440
Every department has a long waiting list.

579
00:45:53,520 --> 00:45:56,000
Why was I given one?

580
00:45:57,840 --> 00:46:00,880
When you applied back then,
you'd just turned eighteen.

581
00:46:00,960 --> 00:46:02,240
Eighteen!

582
00:46:02,320 --> 00:46:05,360
Compared to the rest of us,
you were practically still a child.

583
00:46:05,440 --> 00:46:07,200
There were no other adults at home,

584
00:46:07,280 --> 00:46:09,280
and you had an underage brother
to care for.

585
00:46:09,360 --> 00:46:10,840
Considering all that,

586
00:46:10,920 --> 00:46:16,920
both our hospital and society as a whole
should and must give you priority.

587
00:46:20,440 --> 00:46:23,360
Remember to fill out the forms.
Don't forget.

588
00:46:37,280 --> 00:46:42,040
COMPASSIONATE CARE BED PROGRAM
APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS

589
00:47:17,680 --> 00:47:19,240
Ms. Yang said you might be here.

590
00:47:20,120 --> 00:47:21,240
Sure enough, you are.

591
00:47:23,520 --> 00:47:26,200
I can't believe the hospital rooftop
isn't even locked.

592
00:47:27,320 --> 00:47:29,080
It's supposed to be locked.

593
00:47:29,160 --> 00:47:30,160
As well as the rooftop,

594
00:47:30,760 --> 00:47:33,840
the windows on the upper floors
are also restricted from opening too far.

595
00:47:33,920 --> 00:47:37,600
They're even secured with rivets
to prevent people from jumping.

596
00:47:37,680 --> 00:47:39,400
The hospital would be liable otherwise.

597
00:47:41,320 --> 00:47:43,880
Then how did you find out that
the rooftop wasn't locked?

598
00:47:45,360 --> 00:47:46,960
I stumbled across it by chance.

599
00:47:47,520 --> 00:47:49,840
The lock was really old and had broken.

600
00:47:50,800 --> 00:47:54,080
After that, Ms. Yang and I
would sneak up here to hang laundry.

601
00:47:55,200 --> 00:47:56,720
She loves watching the sunset.

602
00:47:56,800 --> 00:47:59,200
She often takes photos
to share with her online followers.

603
00:48:05,440 --> 00:48:07,240
If only I'd met you all sooner.

604
00:48:10,080 --> 00:48:11,320
That way,

605
00:48:13,120 --> 00:48:14,640
I could've been part of your group.

606
00:48:19,760 --> 00:48:22,680
If you hadn't taken leave
and transferred into our class,

607
00:48:22,760 --> 00:48:24,160
we probably wouldn't have met.

608
00:48:25,680 --> 00:48:27,960
I'd have been busy
taking care of Mom every day,

609
00:48:28,040 --> 00:48:30,760
and you'd have been busy with your paper.

610
00:48:31,640 --> 00:48:35,440
Maybe this is what they mean
by a blessing in disguise.

611
00:48:36,760 --> 00:48:40,000
How do you know it's a blessing?

612
00:48:43,600 --> 00:48:44,800
I believe it is.

613
00:49:23,200 --> 00:49:29,120
THREE YEARS AGO

614
00:50:55,680 --> 00:50:57,560
JIANG MIAN

615
00:51:10,080 --> 00:51:10,920
<i>Zheng Yu.</i>

616
00:51:11,720 --> 00:51:13,080
<i>Why are your eyes so red?</i>

617
00:51:14,160 --> 00:51:16,360
I got dust in my eyes in the stairwell.

618
00:51:17,680 --> 00:51:19,280
By the way, how's Mom doing?

619
00:51:20,080 --> 00:51:23,320
<i>The doctor said her condition is stable</i>
<i>for now, so don't worry.</i>

620
00:54:08,720 --> 00:54:13,720
Subtitle translation by: Cempaka Malinja
